            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for to spend less, then the Mandarin for enough."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 号",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "号 — hào — \"day of the month; number (in a series)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "今天是十月五号 jīntiān shì shíyuè wǔ hào — Today is the fifth of October."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 号 (hào) — five strokes: 口 on top, then a long bar, and under it a stroke that goes down, turns right, turns down again and hooks to the left. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "号 (hào) is inherited from Middle Chinese hawH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'to call', 'a command' and 'a title'. Numbering days and things is not given there, so how it came to that sense is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for reading notices and messages."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
